- Keys: at time 0, value 0; at time `durationMs / 1000`, value 1
- `frameRate` - I can use 60 (default) or any value since I'm using time-based keys

Wait, note 8 says: "A key's time is seconds; its frame is divided by the track's frameRate, else the clip's, which is options.frameRate, else tracks[0].frameRate, else 60. A key with both or neither of time and frame throws."

So I need to use `time` in my keys (in seconds).

Note 14: "fromTime/toTime win over fromFrame/toFrame, and currentTime starts at fromTime. toTime must exceed fromTime or creation throws, so a clip whose keys all sit at time 0 needs a toTime."

Since my keys span from 0 to durationMs/1000, the clip duration will be durationMs/1000. I don't need to pass fromTime/toTime explicitly since the clip duration is > 0.

